{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7EcUdFHFBHHU19QW3sT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft this, a few questions. Your answers will change what the email says:\n\n1. **Do you know why the 97 left?** Was it a survey, replies, or comments at pickup? If it was mostly the hail and how it was handled, the email should open by owning that. If the reasons were mixed (moved away, too much food, Thursdays didn't work), I'd write it differently and give the new pause option more weight.\n2. **Do you want to apologize outright for how the hail weeks were handled?** I mean the missing refunds or credit and the single short email, not the storm itself. Some former members may still be annoyed about it, and naming it plainly is usually what wins people back. I'd like to know how far you're comfortable going.\n3. **Are you offering returning members anything,** like a discount, a bonus week, or early pickup? Or should the case rest on the hail nets, the new field and the pause credit? (I won't invent an offer.)\n4. **How are those 52 open shares likely to go?** Do they usually sell out before March 15? If so, saying that is honest urgency. If not, I'll leave out any \"spots are going fast\" line.\n5. **What are the farm name, your sign-off name and the sign-up link** (or should I leave placeholders)? And do you address members by first name in emails?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":276,"cache_read_input_tokens":9511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":276},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6dea7ef1-15b4-4972-91e7-d20a31bb034f","uuid":"d9ca0b87-434d-4d9c-b3e6-a63a10c9c5e9","timestamp":"202